description=Ever wonder what life was like in the mining boomtowns of old? Wonder no more! Coalfield is a lovingly built recreation of a frontier town, tucked away in Doe Valley Forest just north of Echo Creek. Wet your whistle at the Coalfield Public House or El Grande Saloon, stock up at Porter & Son General Store, and try your hand at the forge in the blacksmith's shop. Rent a room at the Coalfield Inn, pay a visit to the Sheriff's office, and don't miss the hanging post and old graveyard on the west end - just don't ask too many questions about who's buried there!
